   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <opener>
                        <salute>Caro <name type="person" key="rugg87">Ruggiero</name>.</salute>
                    </opener>
                    <p>Ho ricevuto la Sua lettera. Tante grazie</p>
                    <closer>
                        <signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">J.J.</name>
                        </signed>
                    </closer>
                </div>
                <div type="translation">
                    <opener>
                        <salute>Dear Ruggiero. </salute>
                    </opener> <p>I have received your letter. Many thanks </p> <closer>
                        <signed>J.J.</signed>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="global-note1" type="global">This postcard shows a photograph of “Feldkirch Neustadt,” a central street in Feldkirch, Austria, with the Hotel zum Löwen, where the Joyces were staying, visible on the left side of the street. The postcard was produced by L. Heim, a photo publisher in nearby Dornbirn. (JJ sent the same <rs type="letter" key="L_70195">postcard to Ezra Pound on 17 August 1932</rs>.)</note>
            </div>
      </body>
   </text>
